.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt LOGGER 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm logger
.Nd make entries in the system log
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 46Ais
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl H Ar hostname
.Op Fl h Ar host
.Op Fl P Ar port
.Op Fl p Ar pri
.Op Fl S Ar addr Ns Op : Ns Ar port
.Op Fl t Ar tag
.Op Ar message ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility sends a message to
.Xr syslogd 8 :
its arguments, joined by spaces, or else each non-empty line of
.Ar file
or of the standard input as a message of its own.
Messages go to the local log socket
.Pa /dev/log
through
.Xr syslog 3 ,
or with
.Fl h
to another host.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl 4
Use IPv4, which is the only protocol.
.It Fl 6
Use IPv6: not supported, an error.
.It Fl A
With
.Fl h ,
send to every IPv4 address of the host, not only the first.
.It Fl f Ar file
Read the messages from
.Ar file .
.It Fl H Ar hostname
With
.Fl h ,
name this host
.Ar hostname
in the messages, instead of its own name.
.It Fl h Ar host
Send over UDP to
.Xr syslogd 8
on
.Ar host ,
as RFC 3164 messages that name this host.
.It Fl i
Include the process ID of
.Nm
after the tag.
.It Fl P Ar port
With
.Fl h ,
send to
.Ar port ,
a number or
.Cm syslog ,
instead of 514.
.It Fl p Ar pri
Log with priority
.Ar pri ,
given as
.Ar facility . Ns Ar level
with the names of
.Xr syslog.conf 5
.Pq Cm mark No excepted ,
or as a number.
The default is
.Cm user.notice .
.It Fl S Ar addr Ns Op : Ns Ar port
With
.Fl h ,
send from this address and port.
.It Fl s
Also write each message to the standard error.
.It Fl t Ar tag
Tag each message with
.Ar tag
instead of the login name.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
With
.Fl h ,
it fails if a message cannot be sent.
Local messages are handed to
.Xr syslog 3 ,
which reports nothing: when
.Xr syslogd 8
is not running they are lost, and
.Nm
still succeeds.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
logger -p local0.info -t backup "backup finished"
dmesg | logger -t boot -h loghost
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr syslog.conf 5 ,
.Xr syslogd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Bx 4.3 .
This one is OxideBSD's own, written in Rust, with the options of
.Fx .
